Description: FlickOS security kit: forensics
 The Sleuth Kit and Autopsy, binwalk, foremost, scalpel, TestDisk, dc3dd,
 the EWF tools, hashdeep, YARA, ExifTool and steghide from Debian.
 .
 Autopsy is the older web version: it listens on this computer only, while
 it runs. dc3dd and ewfacquire image disks from the command line. Guymager
 isn't part of the kit, because the disk tools it brings start a service;
 Software installs it on its own.
 .
 Use these tools only on computers and networks you own or have permission
 to test.
 .
 A kit is installed from Software's Security Tools and removed there too.
 Nothing it installs runs until it is used
 (docs/design/flickos-security.md).
